    {
      "id": "claim_44210da0eefe47d789c33478f275f3b6",
      "statement": "Registration only binds a DISABLED hook and writes no schedule row: the session normalizes the cadence options, builds a ScheduleHookController whose immutable ctx.props carry the full activation (accountId, workspaceId, scheduleId, spec, cadence), and calls approvalQueue.bindHook with display metadata only — enablement later records the delivery target (workspace + optional gadget), creates the driver row, and arms the alarm via controller.enable; disable removes the row and stored capabilities.",
