    {
      "id": "claim_8d6c05f43b7a446a9855dffcbc8aaf7d",
      "statement": "Delivery per firing: startHook is awaited (not pipelined) because a rejection must skip the occurrence before a callback attempt is counted; admission is a synchronous storage transaction keyed by runId that fences late completions against disabled/re-enabled/revoked schedules; the delivery is authorized as an observation on the returned approval queue; then callback.onSchedule receives {scheduleId, runId, scheduledTime, actualTime, timeZone} — callbacks must be persistent (ctx.restore) and use runId as an idempotency key because delivery may occur more than once.",
      "evidence": [
        {
