    {
      "id": "claim_58215e98345042bd84007a192734dbd8",
      "statement": "Occurrence bounds count due slots, not successful runs (a slot consumes its count as soon as it is due; retries reuse the same runId), so disabling and re-enabling a hook restarts the count; terminal schedules (completed/expired/dead) stay visible and consume enabled-schedule quota until their hook is disabled, and disconnecting the account revokes the driver leaving a permanent tombstone.",
