    {
      "id": "claim_e6c5bd97738c4ce8b680ba1469b47b31",
      "statement": "The scheduler is capability-authorized — it receives no Workshop user identity, does not assert its own ambient policy, exposes no external network authority, and implements no actions (the Workshop's hook admission and observation authorization remain the boundaries) — and it requires the allow_irrevocable_stub_storage compatibility flag while stored callback capabilities exist, which must not be removed from an existing deployment.",
